# SPA fallback: every client route resolves to index.html.
#
# This duplicates the redirect in netlify.toml on purpose. netlify.toml is only
# read when Netlify BUILDS the site from the repository; a manual zip or folder
# upload ignores it entirely. Files in the publish directory — this one and
# _headers — are honoured either way, so the app routes correctly however it got
# deployed.
#
# There is deliberately no rule for /.netlify/functions/*. Netlify rejects any
# redirect whose source starts with /.netlify ("Invalid /.netlify path in
# redirect source") and warns on every deploy. It is also unnecessary: function
# routes are matched before redirects, so the catch-all below cannot swallow
# them.
/*  /index.html  200
